From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: drm/msm/mdp5: flush the CTL before enabling the video timing engine

mdp5_vid_encoder_enable() started the INTF timing engine and only then
flushed the CTL with the configuration of the enabling commit. The first
frame after a CRTC enable therefore scanned out the pipe state left over
from before the disable. On SM-T550 (MSM8916) phoc frees that framebuffer
while the output is off, so most DPMS-on transitions produced a burst of
"Unhandled context fault" at the old iova, an INTF underrun and a "vblank
time out". Flush first, then start the timing engine, as DPU does.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_encoder.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_encoder.c
@@ -163,11 +163,21 @@
 
 	if (WARN_ON(mdp5_encoder->enabled))
 		return;
+
+	/*
+	 * Flush the CTL before the timing engine starts, so the pending pipe,
+	 * mixer and INTF configuration of this commit latches before the first
+	 * frame. Flushed afterwards, the first frame still scans out what the
+	 * pipes held before the CRTC was disabled, typically a framebuffer the
+	 * compositor has freed since: IOMMU faults, an underrun and a vblank
+	 * timeout on DPMS on. DPU does the same ("Video mode must flush CTL
+	 * before enabling timing engine").
+	 */
+	mdp5_ctl_commit(ctl, pipeline, mdp_ctl_flush_mask_encoder(intf), true);
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&mdp5_encoder->intf_lock, flags);
 	mdp5_write(mdp5_kms, REG_MDP5_INTF_TIMING_ENGINE_EN(intfn), 1);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&mdp5_encoder->intf_lock, flags);
-	mdp5_ctl_commit(ctl, pipeline, mdp_ctl_flush_mask_encoder(intf), true);
 
 	mdp5_ctl_set_encoder_state(ctl, pipeline, true);
 
